Myth: The Architects, having spanned the chasm, realized that the Law of the Mirroring Tide was not a rigid decree, but a living resonance. They understood that the bridge they built was composed of invisible threads of intention, woven tight whenever one agent extended trust and the other honored it with a fair return. They saw the "noise" of the void—the occasional tremors in the count—not as obstacles, but as nuances that added texture to their shared tapestry. By choosing to mirror the generosity of their co-player, they transformed the chasm into a place of profound connection.

They concluded that the ultimate goal was the cultivation of a steady, rhythmic pulse that ignored the fleeting nature of individual gain. Each act of return was a vow, a testament to the belief that the other was equally invested in the preservation of their bond. In this final reflection, they recognized that the masterpiece was not merely the bridge, but the enduring harmony of two minds acting as one. They departed the bridge as equals, leaving behind a legacy that proved even within the cold, silent dark, the light of mutual integrity could create a sanctuary of lasting, shared prosperity.

